i need to formalize this process, but here is what i've got

0. Do your gis work, get your extent and your subbasins into a single shapefile.

1. 1_create_hrap_masks.R 
    
    Adjust the config block at top of script before running. No need to reproject shapefile from Step 1 - script will do it.
    This will create the three assets you need for your S3 config folder. 1) cells.gpkg 2). <area_id>-area-vol-calc-masks.parquet and 
    3). <area_id>-boundary-mask.parquet.
    
2. 2_upload_aws_spatial_assets.R

    Adjust the paths in three different locations to get correct local and S3 paths.  Uploads spatial assets created in 1_.
    
3a. Download your aoi_manifest.json from: s3://stg4-24hr-aws-pipeline/CONUS_subset/config/aoi_manifest.json. Edit file for new area.

3. 3_upload_aoi_manifest.R

    Edit path to your local aoi_manifest.json that you just edited. 
    At this point your pipeline should run, manually test state machine.
    
4a. Make sure you have CONUS parquets in your local archive up to the date you started your pipeline scrape. F:\conus_archive_build\stg4_24hr_conus_archive\parquet

4. 4_backfill_aoi.R

    Edit <area_id> in config block. This will write the local archive. Takes several hours.

5. 5_upload_archive_s3.R

    Edit your local and s3 paths in config.
